# The raw source cache: 195 MB of fetched HTML and JSON, all of it
# regenerable from the fetchers. In CI it is restored from the Actions cache
# instead, which gives the same skip-if-present behaviour without putting a
# fifth of a gigabyte of other people's HTML into git history.
data/raw/

# Per-machine, and one of them can hold a key
tracker/config.local.json
tracker/.wrangler/
tracker/dist/
# Generated by build_tracker_page.py from index.template.html + data.js, and
# rebuilt by both CI and any local run - so versioning it guarantees a merge
# conflict on every day both happen. The template is the source; the built
# page is deployed straight from tracker/dist, never read back from git.
tracker/index.html
tracker/champions-ledger.zip
# The seed is GENERATED from inventory/*.json by build_supabase_migration.py,
# and it is a frozen copy of the live ledger: every Pokemon, every build. Once
# Supabase holds the data, a copy in git is a snapshot that drifts from the
# truth and carries personal data for no reason (player, 2026-09-13: "no seria
# mejor borrarlo ya que mis datos de usuario estan en supabase?"). Regenerate
# it when a fresh project needs seeding; do not version the output. Same rule
# the built page already follows.
tracker/supabase_seed.sql
# Supabase CLI scratch state: per-machine, rewritten by every CLI version, and
# it carries the project and organisation ids for no benefit. Nothing reads it
# but the CLI itself.
tracker/supabase/.temp/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.DS_Store
